{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "צפונה", :translit "tzafonah", :gloss "on the north"} {:he "מצפון תפתח הרעה", :translit "mitzafon tiftach hara'ah", :gloss "from the north the evil will open"} {:he "צפון", :translit "tzafun", :gloss "stored away / hidden"} {:he "ואת עורות גדיי העזים", :translit "ve'et orot gedei ha'izim", :gloss "and the skins of the kids of the goats"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word 'tzafon' (north) in the sacrificial law links to 'tzafun' (hidden/stored), connecting the slaughter on the north side to Isaac and Jacob."}], :frame {:text "The verse Jeremiah 1:14 states 'from the north the evil will open,' establishing the north as the direction from which calamity comes. Leviticus 1:11 specifies that certain offerings are slaughtered 'on the north side of the altar.' The rabbinic tradition in Tanhuma (Tazria 8) identifies Isaac's willingness at the Akedah (Genesis 22) as an act whose merit is stored away ('tzafun'); the verse Genesis 22:13 describes the ram sacrificed in Isaac's place. Genesis 27:16 recounts that Jacob used 'the skins of the kids of the goats' to obtain the blessing. Ba'al HaTurim compresses these traditions: the word 'tzafon' (north) in both the sheep and goat sections of the sacrificial laws serves as a protective measure against the evil that opens from the north, by invoking the merits of Isaac (whose ashes are 'stored away') and Jacob (who used goats' skins).", :sources ["Jeremiah 1:14" "Leviticus 1:11" "Genesis 22:13" "Genesis 27:16" "Tanhuma Tazria 8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word 'tzafon' (north) in the sacrificial law links to 'tzafun' (hidden/stored), connecting the slaughter on the north side to Isaac and Jacob.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:21:57.597273204Z", :model "glm-5.2"}